#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:1
msgid "The parameters, and the page that needed each one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:3
msgid ""
"A cell of a configuration table is a short name for a long story. This "
"page tells the stories: one case at a time, with the crop of the page "
"that produced it, and the cell that answers it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:6
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"It is organised by **case** and not by column, because a case is a "
"property of documents and outlives any particular spelling. For the full "
"list of columns a table has, with their defaults, see "
"{doc}`../advanced/structured` and {doc}`../advanced/semistructured`; for "
"what a selection may say, {doc}`../selections`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:11
msgid ""
"Every crop below is from one report — *BlackRock Fixed Income Dublin "
"Funds plc*, 1 261 pages — and every number beside it was measured on that"
" document."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:16
msgid "The holdings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:18
msgid "A name that wraps, and values level with its last line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:20
msgid ""
"Five lines of one instrument name in the third column, with the currency,"
" the nominal and the two figures all level with the last of them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:25
msgid ""
"The instrument's name is one cell, and the generator broke it into five "
"lines with five sets of coordinates. Naming the column that may break "
"**is** asking for the pieces to be put back together — there is no second"
" cell saying \"yes\" — and the direction says which row of the run the "
"rebuilt cell lands on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:20
msgid "What the page shows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:20
msgid "The cell"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:20
msgid "the name occupies several lines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:20
msgid "`Collapse`, the index of the column that breaks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:20
msgid "the figures sit level with the name's **last** line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:20
msgid ""
"`Collapse direction: up`. Level with the **first** would be `down`, the "
"default"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:20
msgid "two tables side by side, so the column of names is **two** columns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:20
msgid ""
"`Collapse: 2 | 7` — the separator is `|`, because a comma is part of a "
"real font name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:36
msgid ""
"The pieces are joined with **nothing** between them, and that is not a "
"choice: a generator breaking at a word boundary leaves the space at the "
"end of the first piece, and breaking inside a word leaves none."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:41
msgid ""
"A lone cell in the column of names is not always a wrapped name. It can "
"be a heading — `Germany (continued)` in the crop above — and "
"geometrically the two are identical: one column filled, the others empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:45
msgid ""
"Here they are **not** identical, because the heading is bold and the "
"names are not, so a body selection on the face excludes it. A format "
"whose headings share the body's face wants no collapse at all, or a "
"deselection that keeps them out of the table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:50
msgid "Where the sub-fund's name is, and where the currency is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:52
#, python-format
msgid ""
"A page head reading BLACKROCK EURO CREDIT ENHANCED INDEX FUND, a date, "
"and the column headings Currency Holdings, Investment, Fair value EUR "
"'000, and % of net asset value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:57
msgid "Three selections, and the third one is the one people get wrong."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:52
#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:131
#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:205
msgid "Cell"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:52
msgid "What it takes here"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:52
msgid "`Subfund set`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:52
msgid ""
"the running head, by face and a band of ordinates: `arial-"
"boldmt[8.5](64:81)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:52
msgid "`Body set`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:52
msgid ""
"`arialmt[8.5]` — the face alone, because nothing else on the page is set "
"in it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:52
msgid "`Currency set`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:52
msgid ""
"the line reading `EUR '000`, which is the heading of the column of "
"**figures**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:65
msgid ""
"The temptation is to take the currency from the `Currency` column, which "
"every row fills in. That column holds the currency the **instrument** is "
"denominated in; on a sub-fund reporting in dollars and holding euro bonds"
" the two are different, and the one the figures are expressed in is the "
"one the output means. `Currency set` is read once per page and the engine"
" finds the code inside whatever text it is given, so the column heading "
"is both honest and sufficient."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:71
msgid "A running head that says `(continued)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:73
msgid ""
"The same crop, two pages later, reads `… INDEX FUND (continued)`, and on "
"1 038 pages of 1 061 it does. Left in, the document has **46** sub-funds "
"instead of 23, and nothing says so: a sub-fund name is an identity, and "
"two spellings are two sub-funds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:77
msgid ""
"`Remove from fund` takes a **regular expression** — `\\(continued\\)` — "
"and is applied before the name becomes that identity. It is a different "
"thing from `Note marks`, which takes a *set of characters* off the end of"
" the name, for the reports that hang a footnote on a sub-fund's title."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:81
msgid "Figures the generator spelled oddly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:83
msgid ""
"Thirty-one amounts in this document carry a **zero-width non-joiner** "
"after the digits. No cell is needed: the engine strips it, reads the "
"number, and writes a line of `out/.log.csv` saying it did —"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:90
msgid ""
"— which is the right shape for this kind of thing. The datum is not lost,"
" and the oddity is not silent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:95
msgid "The statement of net assets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:97
msgid "Why an ordinate band is the wrong anchor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:99
msgid "These two crops are the **same six-page statement**, two pages apart."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:101
msgid ""
"Column headings where each sub-fund title takes two lines, with the year "
"row and the currency row immediately below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:106
msgid ""
"The same headings on another page, where the titles take four lines and "
"the year and currency rows have been pushed much further down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:111
msgid ""
"A sub-fund's title takes one, two, three or four lines according to its "
"length, and **everything below it moves**: the row of currencies sits at "
"109.7 points on the first page, 119.9 two pages later and 143.3 on the "
"last. A `Fund set` written as a band of ordinates read off the first page"
" gives **three** sub-funds of twenty-three, and gives them without an "
"error — the band simply catches the row of years instead, and `2025` is "
"not a currency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:117
msgid "The anchor that holds is written against the **lines**, not the page:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:124
msgid ""
"*The bold, to the right of the column of row labels, from the top margin "
"down to the row that says `'000`, minus the two rows of years.* An "
"anchored side takes the anchor's **inner** edge, and the two subtractions"
" remove what sits in between. The same configuration then reads **23 of "
"23**, and the accounting equation closes on every one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:129
msgid "A window that caught the wrong column"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:131
msgid ""
"The row labelled Net assets attributable to redeemable shareholders, with"
" the note number 14 between the label and the first figure."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:136
msgid ""
"Each amount is read in a window hung off its **own label**: the label's "
"box, displaced by `(dx, dy)` of its own size and scaled by `(width, "
"height)`. One window serves all three amounts on five statements out of "
"eight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:140
msgid ""
"Here it does not. The net-assets row — and only that row — carries the "
"note number `14` between the label and the figures, and the common window"
" takes it: the first sub-fund comes out with net assets of **14**. The "
"correction is one cell, the per-column override, which starts the window "
"past the column of notes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:151
msgid ""
"That is what the per-column cells are for: a statement whose columns "
"differ in one respect and agree in the others."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:154
msgid "Columns that are not sub-funds, and columns that are last year"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:156
msgid ""
"The same statement prints a **combined** column for the whole company, "
"and a previous-financial-year column beside each current one. Two cells, "
"and they say different things:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:131
msgid "What it removes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:131
msgid "`Drop fund set`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:131
msgid ""
"a **column that is not a sub-fund at all**, named by one of its own title"
" lines — here `BlackRock Fixed Income Dublin` — taken away whole, title "
"and figures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:131
msgid "`Drop set`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:131
msgid "the **heading of a column of numbers** to leave out — here `2024`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:164
msgid "A sign that is typography"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:166
msgid ""
"The liabilities are printed `(21,301)`. The brackets are a convention for"
" a deduction, not a negative number, and the schema wants the magnitude "
"because it checks that liabilities plus net assets make the total. That "
"is neither geometry nor meaning but a property of the cast:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:174
msgid ""
"A base — `int` or `float` — and then the conventions the page uses, added"
" with `+`: `dash_as_zero` for a page that writes a dash where the figure "
"is nil, `magnitude` for the sign above. They compose because real "
"statements combine them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:180
msgid "The management company, and the investment managers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:182
msgid "A label that wraps, and the value beside its last line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:184
msgid ""
"A two-column list of related parties: labels on the left, company names "
"on the right, one label wrapping onto a second line that reads Agent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:189
msgid ""
"The value is to the **right** of the label, so the placement is `right` "
"rather than `on_line` — `on_line` is for the reports that write the name "
"*inside* the label's own line, where `After` and `Before` then crop it "
"out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:193
msgid ""
"The subtlety is which line of the label to anchor on. The band the engine"
" opens for a value to the right starts at the label's **top** edge and "
"grows downwards, because a value sits level with its label or below it "
"and never above. Here the rows are tight enough that the *previous* row's"
" value — `BlackRock Asset Management Ireland Limited`, which is the "
"Manager and not the Investment Manager — still overlaps that band, comes "
"first in reading order, and wins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:199
msgid ""
"The label's **last** line is the one level with its value, so that is the"
" anchor: `^Agent:$`, measured as one line on **one** page of 1 261. A "
"page that lost the wrap would carry no `Agent:` and the pipe would fail "
"the page, which is the safe direction to fail in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:203
msgid "A table of delegations, with a cell spanning two rows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:205
msgid ""
"A table of sub-fund names beside their sub-investment managers, where one"
" sub-fund has two managers on two rows and the second row's first column "
"is empty."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:210
msgid ""
"The `table` reader of the investment managers' filter wants one row per "
"sub-fund, with the sub-fund in one column and the manager in another:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:220
msgid ""
"Two of these six sub-funds have **two** delegates, and the second sits on"
" a row of its own with the fund column empty — a cell spanning two rows. "
"Repeating the sub-fund there is reading the layout, so it belongs to "
"`pdf_extract`; without it the second delegate does not appear at all, for"
" either sub-fund, and nothing says so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:225
msgid "Who gets what is left"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:227
msgid ""
"A report states the **exceptions** and leaves the rest implied: unless "
"said otherwise, the manager is the management company. Working out that "
"residual is the filter's real job, and four cells decide it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:205
msgid "On this page"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:205
msgid "`manco`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:205
msgid ""
"`blocks` — the entity that takes the residual is named on this same page,"
" by another pipe of this pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:205
msgid "`emit_manco`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:205
msgid ""
"`never` — that entity is the *Investment Manager*; the management company"
" is declared elsewhere and is not it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:205
msgid "`already_assigned`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:205
msgid "`true` — this page closes the account"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:205
msgid "`funds_include_assigned`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:205
msgid ""
"`false` — the table names sub-funds that no holding of interest touches, "
"and letting them in writes a `funds.csv` row with no provenance"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:238
msgid ""
"The management company's own row, read on a different page, needed two "
"cells of eleven: the label, and `Where: below`. Its `managed_funds` comes"
" out **empty**, which is correct — a report that declares a distinct "
"Investment Manager leaves the management company only a management "
"company."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:244
msgid "The SFDR annex"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:246
msgid "The article is in the box, not in the title"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:248
msgid ""
"The question \"Did this financial product have a sustainable investment "
"objective?\", with an empty box beside Yes and a crossed box beside No."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:253
msgid ""
"The annex of the European periodic template asks the question once and "
"offers two boxes. The ticked one is the answer: affirmative means Article"
" 9, negative Article 8."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:256
msgid ""
"Reading the **title** instead — matching `…referred to in Article 8…` as "
"a substring — works only where the title is there and says so, and across"
" the reference collection and a 905-document corpus the title is "
"**missing on 236 disclosures**. So the box is what is read, and the pipe "
"decides only *where the tick is* and *which label it belongs to*; naming "
"an article is an interpretation of what the question means, and belongs "
"to the next segment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:262
msgid ""
"For a format whose annex is laid out the European way, the whole "
"configuration is **one cell**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:269
msgid ""
"The words of the annex belong to the annex, and the engine knows them in "
"four languages along with five ways of drawing the tick."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:272
msgid "What the marks are, and why they have to be named"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:274
msgid ""
"In the crop the empty box and the crossed one are **glyphs of a symbol "
"font**, and the two green bullets beside them are glyphs of the same font"
" that mean nothing at all. A recogniser that looked for \"a character "
"outside ordinary text\" would be wrong on the second-largest block of "
"disclosures in the corpus, where the **empty** box is the letter `U` and "
"the **ticked** one is the letter `C`: two ordinary letters, "
"indistinguishable by codepoint, with the empty one printed first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:280
msgid ""
"So the table of marks names what counts as ticked, what counts as blank, "
"and — per font — what the only tick is. It carries the measured defaults,"
" and a format may add to all three parts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:283
msgid "When a format has to override one of the annex's own words"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:285
msgid ""
"The `structured` level deliberately does **not** expose the nine anchors "
"of the form. The annex's words are the annex's, not the format's, and a "
"level meant to be *the default guess* is not the place for the cell a "
"format needs when it departs from the standard."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:289
msgid ""
"A format that must override one has measured its page, and it writes a "
"YAML block that can say why. One real case: of four disclosures in a "
"document, the Article 9 one closes the product-name column with "
"`Sustainable Investment Objective`, where the measured wording is "
"`Sustainable investment objective` — the same phrase with one capital "
"letter. A text anchor is a **verbatim** substring, so the column did not "
"close, and the product name ran to the foot of the page and took the "
"module, the percentages and the printed page number with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:306
msgid ""
"**An override replaces the list rather than adding to it**, so all three "
"wordings are written: three of the four disclosures close on the second "
"one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:309
msgid ""
"A name read that way does not produce an error. It produces a sub-fund "
"that does not exist, and the article disappears."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:314
msgid "The ESG indicators"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:316
msgid ""
"A table with the columns Sustainability Indicator, Metric, 2025, 2024 and"
" 2023, one row per indicator, the indicator name wrapping over several "
"lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:321
msgid ""
"The reader keeps the blocks whose **series** and **column** are the ones "
"asked for, takes the block's text as the value, and the block's "
"`indicator` key as the name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:331
msgid ""
"`column: 0` is the rule that the **previous year is not extracted**: this"
" table repeats two previous reference periods, and writing them would "
"mean two indistinguishable rows for the same indicator of the same sub-"
"fund. The columns are numbered **from the most recent**, so the current "
"one is always `0` whatever a document chooses to print beside it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:336
msgid ""
"`series: 0` is the sub-fund's own series. Where a table carries the sub-"
"fund's figures and its benchmark's, the benchmark's row is not a datum of"
" the sub-fund, and the index is what leaves it out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:340
msgid "Whose page is this"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:342
msgid ""
"The question the reader cannot answer by itself, because the answer "
"changes per format: the name may be on the indicators' own page, on the "
"page before, or in a promise an earlier pipe deposited. Four spellings, "
"and the page above is the first:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:316
msgid "`fund:`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:316
msgid "When"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:316
msgid "`blocks`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:316
msgid ""
"the page names its own sub-fund — here the running head does, on all 33 "
"pages of the section"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:316
msgid "`promise`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:316
msgid "one document, one sub-fund"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:316
msgid "`page_promise`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:316
msgid ""
"the name is on the page *n − offset*, keyed by the **printed** page "
"number both pages carry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:316
msgid "absent"
msgstr ""

