msgid ""
"nobody: the section answers in prose, finds no number, and attributing it"
" never arises"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:355
msgid "Two additions this report asked of the engine"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:357
msgid ""
"Both are small, and both are here because the shape of the addition is as"
" instructive as the parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:360
msgid ""
"**A tick the table had not met.** This document answers with a glyph at "
"`U+F0FD`. Wingdings draws four marks on four consecutive codepoints — a "
"check, a cross, a boxed check, a boxed cross — and the measured table "
"held the first and the third. The plain cross and the boxed cross were "
"already ticks, so a cross in a dingbat font is not a new kind of answer: "
"it is the same answer in a font nobody had met. One character, one test."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:366
msgid ""
"Beside it, a second and smaller thing that mattered more: the answer "
"arrives as **two characters in one text object**, the symbol font's own "
"space and then the mark. `U+F020` is byte `0x20` in Wingdings and a space"
" in every sense except Unicode's, so trimming left it in place and the "
"line's first character was not a mark. All four disclosures went unread, "
"with nothing but the pipe's warning to say so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/guides/formats/adding-a-datum/parameters.md:372
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**A sub-fund named on the page itself.** The ESG reader could take its "
"sub-fund from a promise for the whole document, or from the promise of a "
"neighbouring page keyed by the printed page number. Neither says *the "
"running head of this page*, which is what a report whose indicators have "
"a page to themselves provides. The new spelling is `fund: {kind: "
"blocks}`, and it reads the **first non-empty** block of the named type — "
"the same rule the SFDR filter already applies to the product name, and "
"for the same reason: a format may read the title with two pipes of which "
"only one applies to a page."
msgstr ""

